 text+=['','See tradeoffs.json for all-family wins/losses and explicitly identified worst regressions; extrema are illustrations, never favorable-case selection.','']
 for stratum in ['primary','large']:
  v=trade['strata'][stratum]['matched_uniform105'];text.append(f'- {stratum}: queue wins/ties/losses={v["queue_wins"]}/{v["queue_ties"]}/{v["queue_losses"]}; median per-case queue ratio={f(v["median_queue_ratio"],3)}; worst ratio={f(v["max_queue_ratio"],3)}. Queue gain without worse path occurs in{v["queue_gain_without_worse_path"]}/{v["complete_paired_queries"]}completed pairs.')
 text+=['','### Why useful oracle information is not enough','','Safety and resolution are independent bottlenecks. On validation, exact-every-node residuals under the primary pointwise1.05envelope need '+f(ceiling['oracle_fine/heuristic_envelope/1.05']['queue_ops'],1)+'queue operations, versus2108.27for uniform1.05. The same fine information under the full-key2envelope needs '+f(ceiling['oracle_fine/envelope/2.0']['queue_ops'],1)+'. A trusted perfect-admissible cost oracle needs '+f(ceiling['TRUSTED_EXACT_ORACLE/oracle_admissible_anchor/1.0']['queue_ops'],1)+', but its offline reference computation and known admissibility are unavailable to unchecked model outputs.','',
 'Thus even perfect local information can be poorly exploited by a tight envelope. Focal fine-oracle2reduces unique expansions to '+f(ceiling['oracle_fine/focal/2.0']['unique'],1)+'but needs '+f(ceiling['oracle_fine/focal/2.0']['queue_ops'],1)+'queue operations. Neither fewer unique states nor oracle success alone establishes computational improvement. Coarse4x4sample-oracle fields also remain weak, demonstrating information loss inside regions. No new real-model claim is made from these oracle experiments.','',
 '### Late alternatives, including a rejected floating-point artifact','']
