 text+=['The small primary timing advantage over all endpoints is not reproduced against abstention or count-preserving shuffled targets. The pooled queue reduction versus abstention is only about0.4%, nominal/post-hoc, and disappears against stronger geometry/shuffle comparisons; path quality is not better on the large set. This supports no reliable LLM-specific benefit. It is not presented as a new selected algorithm.','',
 '### Conditional relationship to weighted A*','','A separate derivation clarifies the original distance-based scoring. Subtracting the target-dependent constant alpha*d(goal,target) preserves OPEN order. The normalized heuristic divided by1+alpha is consistent and admissible for fixed global alpha>=0with the Euclidean metric. A state-cost induction extends a conservative1+Amax bound to changing GLOBAL weights/targets if every OPEN priority is correctly refreshed and the stated monotone-CLOSED assumptions hold. Thus originalalpha1has a conditional2bound and legacyconstantalpha0.5a1.5bound; lack of ordinary A* optimality must not be confused with necessarily unbounded path cost.','',
 'The argument does not automatically apply to arbitrary node-dependent residuals or stale heuristic keys. LLM-RH* instead uses its explicit pointwise1.05envelope and reopenings. WAYPOINT_BOUND.md states the proof and limitations;756synthetic implementation checks on63reachable small maps pass against independent Shapely Dijkstra. This is analytical interpretation of established weighted search, not claimed invention of a new theorem or a real-LLM performance result.','',
 '### Additional checks and reporting corrections','','The original classical A* emits goal-to-start paths. The shared adapter initially labelled completed paths invalid by expecting the opposite order. paper_denominator_corrected normalizes69completed paths, all independently valid/optimal;31timeouts remain. Time, score, operation/storage counts and original raw files are unchanged. Corrected paper OR/SR summaries use those69completed denominators and explicit coverage. Historical paper-denominator validity summaries should be audited before reuse; original LLM-A*/VM search results are unaffected.','',
 'Development/validation confidence-placement controls preserve sum(delta*confidence) while replacing varying confidence by a constant per query. They produce no convincing general advantage of the reported confidence placement; exact results are retained in confidence_development/validation.json.gz. Confidence is not validated as a probability.','',
 'The final source audit verifies52historical/selected production dependencies against explicit pre-test hashes or the immutable pre-test Git tree, and main remains unchanged. The final209-test suite passes. No extra paid call was issued for these controls.','',
 '![Fixed-hash nested-obstacle illustration; controls ignore the displayed model field.](case_figures/nested.png)','']
